FlatLaf
=======

doccomparator.jar, in the self-contained distributions, holds the classes of FlatLaf
3.7.2 (https://www.formdev.com/flatlaf/), Copyright FormDev Software GmbH, the
window's looks, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Its licence travels
with it, in licenses/FlatLaf-LICENSE.txt of each distribution. The jar published on
Maven Central does not hold it: FlatLaf is a dependency of it there.


Embedded Java runtime
=====================

The self-contained distributions — the Windows and Linux archives — carry a Java runtime
linked (jlink) from the Eclipse Temurin 25 JDK: the modules the program needs, with the
program and FlatLaf among them. The jar published on Maven Central carries no runtime
and is not concerned by this section.

Eclipse Temurin (OpenJDK) is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2,
with the Classpath Exception (GPLv2 + CPE). The Classpath Exception is what permits
distributing DocComparator together with this runtime without affecting the licence of
DocComparator's own code.

The runtime's own licence and notices travel with it, in the jre/legal/ directory of
each distribution:
  - jre/legal/java.base/LICENSE              the GNU General Public License, version 2
  - jre/legal/java.base/ASSEMBLY_EXCEPTION   the Classpath Exception
  - jre/legal/java.base/ADDITIONAL_LICENSE_INFO
  - jre/legal/<module>/*                     the per-component notices of each module
The exact runtime build is recorded in jre/release.

Source code for the OpenJDK runtime is available from:
  - Eclipse Temurin:  https://adoptium.net/temurin/releases/?version=25
  - OpenJDK project:  https://github.com/openjdk/jdk25u


Standard PDF font widths
========================

doccomparator.jar holds org/jtools/doccomparator/pdf/standard-widths.txt: the widths
of the characters of Helvetica and Times, in their four styles, which a PDF may use
without giving them. They are numbers only — no font, no glyph — read by
scripts/standard-widths.py from the font metric (AFM) files of the URW base 35 fonts
Nimbus Sans and Nimbus Roman, made to the same metrics:

  Copyright (URW)++, Copyright 2014 by (URW)++ Design & Development
  Copyright 2015 URW Software
  https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/urw-base35-fonts

Those fonts are distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3,
with a font exception. No font program of theirs is part of DocComparator.


Sample files
============

The documents of samples/ are original, written for this project by
samples/make_samples.py, samples/make_workbooks.py and samples/make_pdfs.py; they fall
under the same licence. The two sample PDFs, printed by LibreOffice, embed subsets of
the Noto Serif fonts (https://notofonts.github.io), licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, version 1.1. The samples are not part of the distributions.
